    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The Constitution of India is the lengthiest of all the written constitutions of the world.",
      "id": "dc1wnr1"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutions are broadly classified into written (such as the US Constitution) and unwritten (such as the British Constitution).",
        "The Constitution of India holds the distinction of being the lengthiest written constitution in the world.",
        "Four key factors influenced its size: India's vast geographical diversity, historical influence of the Government of India Act 1935, a single constitution for both Centre and States, and the dominance of legal luminaries in the Constituent Assembly.",
        "In 1949, it originally contained a Preamble, 395 Articles grouped into 22 Parts, and 8 Schedules.",
        "Through various constitutional amendments, it now comprises a Preamble, around 470 Articles organized into 25 Parts, and 12 Schedules."
      ],
      "id": "i6lh1f4"
    },
