      "content": "<br></br>VERY IMPORTANT: Frequently asked in RRB exams."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sir Ivor Jennings critically referred to the Indian Constitution as having an 'elephantine size' and termed it a 'lawyer's paradise'.",
        "Unlike the United States, India features a single common Constitution governing both the Union and the States.",
        "The structural framework of the Indian Constitution is heavily borrowed from the Government of India Act of 1935."
      ],
      "id": "thz0j47"
